  "notes": "{温|あたた}める means to warm or heat something, particularly food, drinks, or body parts.\n\nTRANSITIVITY:\n- Type: ⟦{他動詞|たどうし}→他動詞：10418_tadoushi⟧ (transitive)\n- Pair: ⟦{温|あたた}まる→温まる：02095_atatamaru⟧ (intransitive) - to become warm\n\nKANJI DISTINCTION:\n- {温|あたた}める: to warm objects, food, body ({温|おん} = temperature)\n- ⟦{暖|あたた}める→暖める：01858_atatameru⟧: to warm rooms, air, atmosphere ({暖|だん} = warmth)\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- ⟦スープ→スープ：00395_suupu⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{温|あたた}める: to heat up soup\n- ⟦{体|からだ}→体：00784_karada⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{温|あたた}める: to warm one's body\n- ⟦{手|て}→手：00569_te⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{温|あたた}める: to warm one's hands\n- ⟦お{弁当|べんとう}→弁当：01014_bentou⟧⟦を→を：00422_wo⟧{温|あたた}める: to heat up a lunch box\n\nCONVENIENCE STORE PHRASE:\n{温|あたた}めます⟦か→か：09473_ka⟧？ 'Shall I heat this up?' - commonly asked when buying food at a ⟦コンビニ→コンビニ：01081_konbini⟧.",
